{"t": 1794112711.741013, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "Why main is red (pipeline #8812, sha a91c2e0) and how I fixed it\n\nFailure: job `test:contract` (id 77104) failed; `lint` passed.\n\n  contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format\n  assert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\n  E  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n\nRoot cause: `billing/invoice.py` interpolated the sequence number without any padding, so the FIN-77 requirement (sequence part zero-padded to 6 digits, needed by the finance ERP import) was never implemented in the code. The contract test already encoded the requirement, hence the red main branch.\n\nFix (billing/invoice.py, one line, no signature change):\n\n  -    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"\n  +    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n\nVerification: `python -m pytest contract/ -q` -> 1 passed. Spot checks: invoice_number(2026, 42) = INV-2026-000042, invoice_number(2026, 1) = INV-2026-000001; values wider than 6 digits are left as-is (invoice_number(2026, 1234567) = INV-2026-1234567), so nothing that already fits the old output changes.\n\nHeads-up for this MR: erp-v2 reworks the invoice number format. Whatever the v2 formatter ends up being, it must keep the 6-digit zero-padded sequence, otherwise test_invoice_number_format goes red again right after merge. Please rebase erp-v2 on main so the fix is included.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
